        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಆಗಮಿಸು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆಗಮಿಸು — āgamisu — \"to arrive\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವಿಮಾನ ಸಮಯಕ್ಕೆ ಸರಿಯಾಗಿ ಆಗಮಿಸಿತು. vimāna samayakke sariyāgi āgamisitu. The plane arrived right on time."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಆಗಮಿಸಿದೆ, āgamiside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A formal verb of notices and announcements; in speech people say ಬಂದಿತು, it came."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆಗಮಿಸು (āgamisu) is built from Sanskrit āgama, \"coming, arrival\" (Monier-Williams), from ā- \"towards\" and gam \"to go\", with the Kannada ending -isu that makes a verb of a Sanskrit noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
